 "body_html": "<p>Why does modifying a pre-initialized string literal cause a segmentation fault? For example: </p>\n\n<pre><code>char *str = \"Hello world\";\nstr[0] = 'h'; \n</code></pre>\n\n<p>When you initialize <code>str</code> to that string value, doesn't the compiler automatically allocate memory for that string constant, assign its starting location to <code>str</code> and free it upon program exit? </p>\n",
 "passes": [
  "main"
 ],
